  "tagline": "Strongly typed entity-relation database with TypeQL, polymorphic queries and a Rust core.",
  "description": "TypeDB (formerly Grakn, developed by the company previously called Vaticle) models data as typed entities, n-ary relations and attributes with inheritance, and queries it in TypeQL, a declarative pattern language that supports polymorphic queries and user-defined functions. Version 3.0 rewrote the engine in Rust, and 3.x releases ship frequently (3.14.1 in October 2026). It sits between graph and relational: richer type semantics than a property graph, without SQL tables. It is compelling for complex domain models (cybersecurity, biomedical, engineering) and less so for teams that want a mainstream query language.",
